const topics = [];
// Each bilingual field uses a tab separator; pipes are reserved for answer keywords.
const pair = (text) => text.split("\t");
function add(slug, section, level, title, definition, mechanism, example, trap, question, correct, wrong, keywords, book) {
 const id = `u4-${String(topics.length + 1).padStart(2, "0")}-${slug}`;
 topics.push({ id, section, level, title: pair(title), definition: pair(definition), mechanism: pair(mechanism), example: pair(example), trap: pair(trap), question: pair(question), correct: pair(correct), wrong: wrong.map(pair), keywords, book });
}
add("trade-benefits", "4.1", "core", "贸易、专业化与竞争\tTrade, specialisation and competition",
 "国际贸易通过专业化、更大市场、竞争和技术传播扩大消费选择，但收益分配不均。\tTrade can widen consumption choices through specialisation, larger markets, competition and technology diffusion, but gains are unevenly distributed.",
 "更大市场支持专业化；规模扩大可降低平均成本；竞争约束价格并促进创新\tLarger markets support specialisation; greater scale can reduce average costs; competition can restrain prices and encourage innovation",
 "原创假设：本国药品企业进入更大市场，分摊研发成本；消费者可能获得低价药，但低效率企业的工人可能需要转岗。\tHypothetical scenario: a medicine producer spreads research costs across a larger market. Consumers may obtain cheaper medicines while workers in less efficient firms face retraining.",
 "总收益增加不代表每个人都获益；调整成本、环境成本和依赖性需要单独评价。\tAggregate gains do not mean everyone gains; adjustment costs, environmental effects and dependence require separate evaluation.",
 "更大出口市场如何帮助降低单位成本？\tHow can a larger export market reduce unit costs?", "分摊固定成本\tSpreading fixed costs", ["必然消除所有失业\tNecessarily removing all unemployment", "使资源不再稀缺\tEnding resource scarcity", "保证每家企业盈利\tGuaranteeing profit for every firm"], ["专业化|specialisation", "规模|scale", "竞争|competition"]);
add("free-trade-imports", "4.1", "core", "小国自由贸易与进口\tFree trade and imports in a small economy",
 "在同质商品、小国和无运输成本模型中，世界价格低于自给均衡价时，国内需求超过供给，差额为进口。\tIn a small-country model with homogeneous goods and no transport costs, a world price below the autarky price creates imports equal to domestic demand minus supply.",
 "世界价格低于自给价；国内消费增加而生产减少；进口满足需求与供给差额\tThe world price is below autarky; domestic consumption rises and production falls; imports fill the demand-supply gap",
 "原创假设：Pw=10 时 Qd=100、Qs=40，进口 60；消费者获益而生产者受损，在无外部性模型中存在净福利收益。\tHypothetical scenario: at Pw=10, Qd=100 and Qs=40, so imports are 60. Consumers gain and producers lose, with net welfare gains in a model without externalities.",
 "小国接受世界价格；进口量不是国内总消费量。\tA small economy takes the world price; imports are not total domestic consumption.",
 "Qd=90、Qs=30 时进口量是多少？\tWith Qd=90 and Qs=30, how large are imports?", "60\t60", ["120\t120", "90\t90", "30\t30"], ["世界价格|world price", "进口|imports", "差额|gap"]);
add("free-trade-exports", "4.1", "core", "小国自由贸易与出口\tFree trade and exports in a small economy",
 "世界价格高于自给均衡价时，国内供给超过需求，剩余产出出口。\tWhen the world price exceeds the autarky equilibrium price, domestic supply exceeds demand and the surplus is exported.",
 "较高世界价格提高生产激励；国内消费者减少购买；出口等于供给减需求\tA higher world price encourages production; domestic consumers buy less; exports equal supply minus demand",
 "原创假设：Pw=20 时 Qs=120、Qd=70，出口 50；生产者获益，国内消费者支付更高价格。\tHypothetical scenario: at Pw=20, Qs=120 and Qd=70, so exports are 50. Producers gain while domestic consumers pay a higher price.",
 "出口收益不是纯福利收益；应比较消费者与生产者剩余的变化。\tExport receipts are not pure welfare gains; compare changes in consumer and producer surplus.",
 "Qs=80、Qd=50，出口多少？\tIf Qs=80 and Qd=50, what are exports?", "30\t30", ["130\t130", "50\t50", "80\t80"], ["世界价格|world price", "出口|exports", "供给|supply"]);
add("absolute-advantage", "4.1", "hl", "绝对优势\tAbsolute advantage",
 "使用相同资源能够生产更多某产品，或生产同量产品所需资源更少，即拥有绝对优势。\tAbsolute advantage means producing more of a good with the same resources, or using fewer resources for the same output.",
 "保持投入可比；比较单位资源的产量；识别生产率优势\tHold inputs comparable; compare output per unit of resources; identify the productivity advantage",
 "原创假设：每工时 A 可产 8 件布，B 可产 5 件，A 在布上有绝对优势；仍需比较另一商品才能判断比较优势。\tHypothetical scenario: A produces eight cloth units per hour and B five. A has absolute advantage in cloth, but another good is needed to establish comparative advantage.",
 "绝对优势比较生产率，比较优势比较机会成本，二者不能互换。\tAbsolute advantage compares productivity; comparative advantage compares opportunity cost.",
 "同一工时产量 8 对 5，谁有绝对优势？\tWith output of eight versus five per equal hour, who has absolute advantage?", "产量为 8 的经济体\tThe economy producing eight", ["产量为 5 的经济体\tThe economy producing five", "必然都没有\tNeither necessarily", "只看汇率判断\tDecide only from the exchange rate"], ["资源|resources", "产量|output", "生产率|productivity"], ["14", "14.2", 438]);
add("comparative-advantage", "4.1", "hl", "比较优势与贸易区间\tComparative advantage and the trading interval",
 "比较优势是较低机会成本；互利交换比率须位于双方机会成本之间，且须考虑模型假设。\tComparative advantage means lower opportunity cost. A mutually beneficial trading ratio lies between the two opportunity costs, subject to model assumptions.",
 "计算放弃的另一商品；比较机会成本；在两者之间确定互利交换比率\tCalculate the other good forgone; compare opportunity costs; choose a trading ratio between them",
 "原创假设：A 可产 10 布或 20 粮，B 可产 6 布或 18 粮。1 布成本分别为 2 粮、3 粮；A 专业化布，按 1 布换 2.5 粮双方可获益。假设资源可转移、充分就业且忽略运费。\tHypothetical scenario: A can make ten cloth or twenty grain; B six cloth or eighteen grain. One cloth costs two grain in A and three in B. A specialises in cloth; trading at 2.5 grain per cloth can benefit both. Assume mobile domestic resources, full employment and no freight costs.",
 "即使一国两种商品都有绝对优势，仍可在不同机会成本下互利贸易；现实调整和外部性可能削弱收益。\tEven an economy with absolute advantage in both goods can gain from different opportunity costs; adjustment and externalities can weaken gains.",
 "两国 1 布成本为 2 粮和 3 粮，哪个比率可能互利？\tIf one cloth costs two and three grain respectively, which ratio can benefit both?", "1 布换 2.5 粮\tOne cloth for 2.5 grain", ["1 布换 1 粮\tOne cloth for one grain", "1 布换 4 粮\tOne cloth for four grain", "机会成本相同时必有专业化收益\tEqual opportunity costs guarantee specialisation gains"], ["机会成本|opportunity cost", "专业化|specialisation", "交换比率|trading ratio"], ["14", "14.2", 438]);
add("trade-evaluation", "4.1", "core", "贸易收益的条件与分配\tConditions and distribution of trade gains",
 "贸易能提高配置效率，但长期发展收益取决于产业联系、技能、市场势力和收入分配。\tTrade can improve allocative efficiency, while long-run development gains depend on linkages, skills, market power and distribution.",
 "进口竞争促使资源重新配置；部分企业和工人承担调整成本；再培训与社会保障影响净收益分布\tImport competition reallocates resources; some firms and workers bear adjustment costs; retraining and social protection affect the distribution of net gains",
 "原创假设：廉价进口降低家庭支出，但偏远地区唯一工厂关闭；就业转移需要时间，不能用全国净收益否定地区损失。\tHypothetical scenario: cheaper imports lower household spending but close a remote region's only factory. Reallocation takes time; national net gains do not erase local losses.",
 "把所有进口都视为损失，或把所有贸易都视为人人受益，都会遗漏利益相关者。\tTreating every import as a loss, or all trade as beneficial to everyone, omits stakeholders.",
 "评价贸易开放最应补充哪个问题？\tWhich question best extends an evaluation of trade opening?", "谁获益、谁付出调整成本\tWho gains and who bears adjustment costs", ["出口是否永远越多越好\tWhether more exports are always better", "为何消费者剩余必为零\tWhy consumer surplus must be zero", "为何不再需要生产要素\tWhy factors of production are no longer needed"], ["效率|efficiency", "调整|adjustment", "分配|distribution"]);
add("tariff", "4.2", "core", "关税与小国福利\tTariffs and small-country welfare",
 "关税是进口税；小国单位关税把国内价从 Pw 提高至 Pw+t，降低进口并产生税收与效率损失。\tA tariff taxes imports. In a small economy a specific tariff raises domestic price from Pw to Pw+t, reduces imports and creates revenue and efficiency losses.",
 "进口成本提高；国内生产增加消费减少；政府按税后进口量征税\tImport costs rise; domestic production rises and consumption falls; revenue is levied on post-tariff imports",
 "原创假设：Pw=10，税 t=2，税后 Qd=90、Qs=50，进口 40，税收 80。无外部性和报复时仍有生产与消费扭曲损失。\tHypothetical scenario: Pw=10, t=2, post-tariff Qd=90 and Qs=50. Imports are 40 and revenue 80. Production and consumption distortions remain even without externalities or retaliation.",
 "关税收入应乘税后进口量；它是转移，不等于净福利增加。\tUse post-tariff imports for revenue; revenue is a transfer, not a net welfare gain.",
 "单位关税 3，税后进口 20，税收多少？\tA tariff of three with post-tariff imports of twenty yields what revenue?", "60\t60", ["23\t23", "17\t17", "必须用税前进口量\tThe pre-tariff import volume must be used"], ["关税|tariff", "进口|imports", "税收|revenue"]);
add("quota", "4.2", "core", "进口配额与配额租\tImport quotas and quota rents",
 "配额直接限制进口数量，通常抬高国内价格；价格差形成配额租，归属取决于许可分配。\tA quota directly limits imports and normally raises domestic price. The price gap creates quota rents whose recipients depend on licence allocation.",
 "进口数量受限；国内稀缺性推高价格；许可证持有人获得配额租\tImports are capped; scarcity raises domestic price; licence holders receive quota rents",
 "原创假设：世界价 10、国内价 14，配额 30，配额租为 120。政府拍卖许可可能获得收入，免费给外国出口商则租可能流向国外。\tHypothetical scenario: world price ten, domestic price fourteen and quota thirty create rents of 120. Auctions may generate public revenue; free licences to foreign exporters can transfer rents abroad.",
 "配额租不会自动归本国政府；需求增加时配额还可能带来更大涨价。\tQuota rents do not automatically accrue to the home government; a demand increase can further raise price under a fixed quota.",
 "配额许可免费给外国出口商，租最可能归谁？\tWho may receive rents if quota licences are freely given to foreign exporters?", "外国许可证持有人\tForeign licence holders", ["必定归本国财政\tAlways the home treasury", "必定归所有消费者\tAlways all consumers", "租必定为零\tRents must be zero"], ["数量|quantity", "许可证|licences", "配额租|quota rents"]);
add("production-subsidy", "4.2", "core", "生产补贴与进口替代\tProduction subsidies and import displacement",
 "小国对国内生产提供补贴可增加国内供给、减少进口；消费者仍按世界价购买，财政承担补贴成本。\tA domestic production subsidy in a small economy can increase domestic supply and reduce imports. Consumers still buy at the world price and the government funds the subsidy.",
 "生产者每单位净收入增加；国内供给扩大；进口减少但消费价不必提高\tProducer receipts per unit rise; domestic supply expands; imports fall without a necessary rise in consumer price",
 "原创假设：补贴 2、国内产量由 40 增至 60，总成本 120，而非仅对新增 20 单位补贴。模型假定持续进口且世界价不变。\tHypothetical scenario: a subsidy of two raises domestic output from forty to sixty, costing 120, not merely subsidising the twenty extra units. Imports remain positive and the world price is fixed.",
 "补贴未必提高消费者价格；政府机会成本与低效率生产仍需评价。\tA subsidy need not raise consumer price; fiscal opportunity cost and inefficient production still matter.",
 "补贴 4，补贴后国内总产量 30，财政成本？\tA subsidy of four on total domestic output of thirty costs how much?", "120\t120", ["仅补新增产量\tOnly subsidise additional output", "34\t34", "26\t26"], ["补贴|subsidy", "供给|supply", "财政成本|fiscal cost"]);
add("export-subsidy", "4.2", "hl", "出口补贴\tExport subsidies",
 "出口补贴按出口量支付，可能提高本国价格并扩大出口，财政支出和国内消费损失影响福利。\tAn export subsidy pays per exported unit and can raise the domestic price and exports; fiscal costs and domestic consumption losses affect welfare.",
 "出口每单位回报提高；生产者转向出口直到国内价调整；国内生产增加消费下降\tReturns per exported unit rise; producers divert sales until domestic price adjusts; domestic output rises and consumption falls",
 "原创假设：小国世界价 10、出口补贴 2，在可自由转售的简化模型下国内价升至 12；若出口 50，财政成本为 100。\tHypothetical scenario: with world price ten and an export subsidy of two, domestic price rises to twelve in a simplified arbitrage model. Fifty exports cost the government 100.",
 "出口增加不是净福利增加；补贴也可能引发贸易争端，具体规则须核验。\tMore exports do not establish a welfare gain; subsidies can also trigger trade disputes, whose specific rules require verification.",
 "出口补贴 2、出口 50，财政支出多少？\tAn export subsidy of two on fifty exports costs how much?", "100\t100", ["52\t52", "48\t48", "必然没有成本\tNecessarily no cost"], ["出口|exports", "补贴|subsidy", "消费|consumption"]);
add("administrative-barriers", "4.2", "core", "行政壁垒与标准\tAdministrative barriers and standards",
 "繁复手续、采购偏好或歧视性标准可增加进口成本；正当健康与环境标准也可能纠正市场失灵。\tComplex procedures, procurement preferences or discriminatory standards can raise import costs; legitimate health and environmental standards may correct market failure.",
 "合规时间和费用提高；进口供给受限；保护收益与公共利益须分别判断\tCompliance time and costs rise; imports are constrained; protection gains and public benefits need separate assessment",
 "原创假设：同样食品安全风险，若进口商被要求重复检验而本地企业无需检验，应评估必要性、证据与非歧视性。\tHypothetical scenario: importers face duplicate inspections while local firms with identical food risks do not. Assess necessity, evidence and non-discrimination.",
 "不能因为某标准减少进口就断言它毫无公共利益，也不能忽略隐性歧视。\tLower imports alone do not prove a standard lacks public value, but hidden discrimination must not be ignored.",
 "评价进口检验要求最相关的标准是什么？\tWhat matters most when evaluating import inspections?", "是否必要且非歧视\tWhether they are necessary and non-discriminatory", ["进口越少越有效率\tFewer imports always mean more efficiency", "所有标准都应取消\tEvery standard should be removed", "只看文件页数\tOnly count pages of paperwork"], ["合规|compliance", "成本|costs", "歧视|discrimination"]);
add("infant-industry", "4.3", "core", "幼稚产业与战略保护\tInfant industries and strategic protection",
 "暂时保护可能帮助有学习外部性的产业形成竞争力，但须证明未来收益超过当前成本并设置退出条件。\tTemporary protection may help industries with learning spillovers become competitive, provided future gains exceed current costs and exit conditions are credible.",
 "初期规模小成本高；学习与规模扩大降低成本；到期撤销保护检验竞争力\tSmall initial scale raises costs; learning and scale reduce costs; removing protection tests competitiveness",
 "原创假设：设备产业获三年支持，续期取决于单位成本下降和出口表现；没有绩效条件可能把补贴固化。\tHypothetical scenario: equipment firms receive three years of support, conditional on lower unit costs and export performance. Unconditional renewal can entrench subsidies.",
 "产业新不等于值得保护；政府信息不足、寻租和报复可能使净收益为负。\tBeing new does not justify protection; poor information, rent seeking and retaliation may outweigh gains.",
 "什么最能增强幼稚产业论据？\tWhat most strengthens the infant-industry case?", "可验证的学习外部性与退出期限\tVerifiable learning spillovers and a sunset date", ["永久保护承诺\tA promise of permanent protection", "完全不考核成本\tNo cost evaluation", "企业亏损本身\tLosses alone"], ["学习|learning", "成本|costs", "退出|exit"]);
add("protection-arguments", "4.3", "core", "就业、安全与反倾销论据\tEmployment, security and anti-dumping arguments",
 "贸易保护可维护特定岗位或战略供应，但会提高投入成本、影响出口并可能引发报复；倾销不能仅由低价推断。\tProtection may preserve particular jobs or strategic supplies but raises input costs, affects exports and risks retaliation. A low price alone does not establish dumping.",
 "进口竞争冲击特定产业；保护减缓调整；下游成本与报复影响其他岗位\tImport competition hits particular industries; protection slows adjustment; input costs and retaliation affect jobs elsewhere",
 "原创假设：钢铁关税保住部分炼钢岗位，却提高机械企业成本；评价需比较净就业、供应韧性与再培训方案。\tHypothetical scenario: a steel tariff preserves some steel jobs but raises machinery producers' costs. Evaluate net jobs, supply resilience and retraining alternatives.",
 "不能把受保护行业岗位当作净就业效果，也不能把低工资直接等同于不公平竞争。\tProtected-sector jobs are not the net employment effect; low wages do not by themselves establish unfair competition.",
 "钢铁关税评价还应考虑谁？\tWhose position also matters in evaluating a steel tariff?", "使用钢材的下游企业\tDownstream firms using steel", ["仅钢铁生产者\tOnly steel producers", "只看关税名称\tOnly the tariff's name", "忽略贸易伙伴\tIgnore trading partners"], ["就业|employment", "成本|costs", "报复|retaliation"]);
add("protection-evaluation", "4.3", "core", "保护政策的综合评价\tEvaluating protection policies",
 "评价保护应比较效率、公平、财政成本、外部性、时限及贸易伙伴反应，并与针对性替代政策比较。\tEvaluate protection through efficiency, equity, fiscal costs, externalities, duration and partner responses, alongside targeted alternatives.",
 "确定政策目标；比较各方收益与成本；依据条件和替代方案作判断\tSpecify the objective; compare stakeholder gains and costs; judge using conditions and alternatives",
 "原创假设：衰退地区需要支持，可比较关税、工资保险与培训；若问题是技能错配，培训可能比长期高价保护更直接。\tHypothetical scenario: compare tariffs, wage insurance and training for a declining region. If skill mismatch is the problem, training may address it more directly than prolonged price protection.",
 "小国净福利损失结论依赖模型；外部性或大国贸易条件效应应另行论证，不能随意套用。\tSmall-country welfare losses are model-dependent; externalities or large-country terms-of-trade effects require separate arguments.",
 "评价保护政策时最完整的做法是什么？\tWhich approach best evaluates protection?", "将目标、成本、条件与替代措施连接\tLink objectives, costs, conditions and alternatives", ["只计算生产者收益\tCount only producer gains", "认为短期等于长期\tTreat short run as long run", "把税收当纯福利增量\tTreat revenue as a pure welfare gain"], ["效率|efficiency", "公平|equity", "替代|alternatives"]);
add("wto", "4.3", "core", "世界贸易组织与合作\tThe WTO and trade cooperation",
 "WTO 为成员贸易规则、谈判、透明度与争端解决提供制度框架；规则合作可降低不确定性，但利益与执行能力不均。\tThe WTO provides a framework for members' trade rules, negotiations, transparency and dispute settlement. Cooperation can reduce uncertainty, though interests and enforcement capacity differ.",
 "成员承诺规则；透明度降低政策不确定性；协商与争端程序处理冲突\tMembers commit to rules; transparency reduces policy uncertainty; negotiation and dispute procedures address conflict",
 "原创假设：两国就进口限制产生分歧，共同规则可使争论围绕证据；小经济体仍可能面临法律资源不足。\tHypothetical scenario: common rules focus a dispute over import restrictions on evidence, while a small economy may lack legal resources.",
 "WTO 不是世界政府，也不保证所有贸易壁垒消失；当前争端机构运行状态须查官方资料。\tThe WTO is not a world government and does not remove every barrier; current dispute-body operations require official verification.",
 "规则透明度如何帮助贸易？\tHow can rule transparency support trade?", "降低政策不确定性\tReduce policy uncertainty", ["保证每个争端立即解决\tGuarantee instant resolution of every dispute", "替代所有国内政策\tReplace all domestic policy", "固定所有汇率\tFix every exchange rate"], ["规则|rules", "透明度|transparency", "争端|dispute"], ["15", "15.4", 483]);
add("trading-blocs", "4.4", "core", "优惠协定、自由贸易区与关税同盟\tPreferential agreements, free trade areas and customs unions",
 "优惠协定降低部分成员壁垒；自由贸易区取消成员间贸易壁垒但保留各自对外关税；关税同盟另有共同对外关税。\tPreferential agreements reduce selected member barriers. Free trade areas remove internal barriers while retaining separate external tariffs; customs unions add a common external tariff.",
 "成员降低内部壁垒；自由贸易区需原产地规则；共同对外关税形成关税同盟\tMembers lower internal barriers; free trade areas need rules of origin; a common external tariff creates a customs union",
 "原创假设：A 与 B 内部免税但对 C 税率不同，属于自由贸易区；原产地规则防止经最低税率成员转运规避关税。\tHypothetical scenario: A and B trade duty-free but tax C differently. This is a free trade area; rules of origin limit tariff circumvention through the lowest-tariff member.",
 "内部自由贸易本身不意味着共同对外关税或共同货币。\tInternal free trade alone does not imply a common external tariff or currency.",
 "自由贸易区与关税同盟的关键差别是什么？\tWhat chiefly distinguishes a customs union from a free trade area?", "共同对外关税\tA common external tariff", ["必须共同货币\tA compulsory common currency", "必须相同人口\tIdentical populations", "禁止内部贸易\tBanning internal trade"], ["内部|internal", "对外关税|external tariff", "原产地|origin"]);
add("common-market", "4.4", "core", "共同市场与经济一体化\tCommon markets and economic integration",
 "共同市场在贸易一体化基础上允许生产要素跨成员流动；更深一体化涉及政策协调和自主权权衡。\tA common market adds factor mobility to trade integration. Deeper integration brings policy coordination and trade-offs over autonomy.",
 "壁垒下降扩展市场；劳动资本流向回报较高处；协调政策降低跨境摩擦\tLower barriers expand markets; labour and capital move toward higher returns; policy coordination reduces cross-border frictions",
 "原创假设：工程师跨成员就业改善技能匹配，但人才流出地区可能失去税基，资格互认与公共服务协调因此重要。\tHypothetical scenario: engineers moving between members improve skill matching, while origin regions may lose tax revenue. Qualification recognition and service coordination matter.",
 "要素自由流动不保证地区收益均衡；基础设施和制度差异仍存在。\tFactor mobility does not ensure equal regional gains; infrastructure and institutional differences remain.",
 "共同市场在关税同盟基础上增加什么？\tWhat does a common market add to a customs union?", "生产要素流动\tFactor mobility", ["必然无失业\tGuaranteed zero unemployment", "世界统一价格\tA single price for everything worldwide", "禁止迁移\tA ban on migration"], ["要素|factors", "流动|mobility", "协调|coordination"]);
add("trade-creation-diversion", "4.4", "hl", "贸易创造与贸易转移\tTrade creation and trade diversion",
 "贸易创造以低成本成员进口替代高成本本国产出；贸易转移则以较高成本成员进口替代低成本非成员进口。\tTrade creation replaces costly domestic output with cheaper member imports. Trade diversion replaces cheaper non-member imports with higher-cost member imports.",
 "内部关税取消改变相对价格；采购来源改变；比较真实资源成本与关税收入变化\tRemoving internal tariffs changes relative prices; sourcing changes; compare real resource costs and tariff revenue changes",
 "原创假设：非成员成本 8、成员成本 10，对外税 4。入盟后免税成员价 10 低于非成员含税价 12，转向成员属于贸易转移。\tHypothetical scenario: a non-member costs eight and a member ten; the external tariff is four. After integration, the member price ten undercuts the non-member landed price twelve. Switching is trade diversion.",
 "消费者价格降低不充分证明全球配置效率提高；还要看供应者真实成本。\tA lower consumer price alone does not establish better global allocation; compare suppliers' real costs.",
 "从成本 8 的非成员转向成本 10 的成员，属于什么？\tSwitching from a non-member costing eight to a member costing ten is what?", "贸易转移\tTrade diversion", ["贸易创造\tTrade creation", "绝对优势自动提高\tAutomatically higher absolute advantage", "货币贬值\tCurrency depreciation"], ["成本|costs", "成员|member", "转移|diversion"]);
add("monetary-union", "4.4", "core", "货币联盟的收益与代价\tBenefits and costs of monetary union",
 "货币联盟采用共同货币和共同货币政策，减少内部汇兑成本与汇率风险，但成员失去独立利率和汇率调整工具。\tA monetary union uses a common currency and monetary policy, reducing internal conversion costs and exchange risk while removing independent interest-rate and exchange-rate adjustment.",
 "共同货币降低交易摩擦；价格比较更容易；非对称冲击下统一利率可能不适合所有成员\tA shared currency lowers transaction frictions; price comparison becomes easier; one interest rate may not suit members facing asymmetric shocks",
 "原创假设：A 经济过热而 B 衰退，同一利率难以兼顾；劳动力流动、财政转移与价格工资弹性影响调整能力。\tHypothetical scenario: A overheats while B is in recession, so one rate is hard to tailor. Labour mobility, fiscal transfers and price-wage flexibility affect adjustment.",
 "共同货币不自动带来财政联盟，也不消除成员信用风险。\tA common currency does not automatically create a fiscal union or eliminate member credit risk.",
 "面对非对称冲击，成员失去了哪项工具？\tWhich tool does a member lose when facing an asymmetric shock?", "独立本币贬值\tIndependent currency depreciation", ["所有财政支出\tAll fiscal expenditure", "所有劳动流动\tAll labour mobility", "一切贸易\tAll trade"], ["货币|currency", "利率|interest rate", "冲击|shock"], ["15", "15.3", 482]);
add("integration-evaluation", "4.4", "hl", "一体化的动态评价\tDynamic evaluation of integration",
 "经济一体化可能增强竞争、投资和规模经济；收益取决于成员差异、制度质量与贸易创造相对转移。\tIntegration may strengthen competition, investment and scale economies. Gains depend on member differences, institutional quality and trade creation relative to diversion.",
 "市场扩大吸引投资；竞争促进生产率；地区集中和政策约束改变分配\tA larger market attracts investment; competition encourages productivity; regional concentration and policy constraints alter distribution",
 "原创假设：共同市场吸引汽车投资，但就业集中在港口地区；评估时加入地区基金、技能和跨境公共品，而非只看贸易总额。\tHypothetical scenario: a common market attracts car investment, concentrated near ports. Evaluate regional funds, skills and cross-border public goods alongside trade volumes.",
 "更多区域内贸易也可能来自转移，不能仅凭贸易量宣告福利提高。\tMore intraregional trade can reflect diversion; volumes alone do not establish welfare gains.",
 "哪项最能支持长期一体化收益？\tWhat most supports long-run integration gains?", "竞争与技能投资提高生产率\tCompetition and skill investment raise productivity", ["贸易量增加就足够\tHigher trade volume alone suffices", "永久保护所有低效企业\tPermanently protecting every inefficient firm", "不需协调制度\tNo institutional coordination is needed"], ["投资|investment", "生产率|productivity", "分配|distribution"]);
add("floating-exchange-rate", "4.5", "core", "浮动汇率与报价方向\tFloating exchange rates and quotation",
 "汇率是一种货币以另一种货币表示的价格；以美元每本币报价时，数值上升表示本币升值。\tAn exchange rate is one currency's price in another. With dollars per home currency unit, a rise means home-currency appreciation.",
 "先定义报价单位；外汇需求与供给交点确定汇率；比较同一报价下的新旧价格\tDefine quotation units; currency demand and supply determine equilibrium; compare prices using the same quotation",
 "原创假设：1 本币从 0.50 美元变为 0.60 美元，本币升值 20%；倒数报价从每美元 2 本币变为约 1.67，百分比并不对称。\tHypothetical scenario: one home unit rises from 0.50 to 0.60 dollars, a 20% appreciation. The inverse falls from two home units per dollar to about 1.67; percentage changes are not symmetric.",
 "不先说明分子分母，汇率上升可能被误读；浮动制称升值或贬值。\tWithout stating numerator and denominator, a rising rate can be misread; floating-rate changes are appreciation or depreciation.",
 "美元每本币从 0.4 到 0.5，发生什么？\tDollars per home unit rise from 0.4 to 0.5. What happens?", "本币升值 25%\tHome currency appreciates 25%", ["本币贬值 25%\tHome currency depreciates 25%", "本币升值 20%\tHome currency appreciates 20%", "报价毫无意义\tThe quotation has no meaning"], ["报价|quotation", "需求|demand", "升值|appreciation"]);
add("currency-demand-supply", "4.5", "core", "外汇需求与供给的决定因素\tDeterminants of currency demand and supply",
 "外国购买本国出口和资产形成对本币需求；本国购买进口和外国资产形成本币供给。\tForeign purchases of home exports and assets create demand for home currency; home purchases of imports and foreign assets create its supply.",
 "外国需求或相对回报改变；本币需求或供给移动；浮动汇率调整\tForeign demand or relative returns change; home-currency demand or supply shifts; the floating rate adjusts",
 "原创假设：在风险与预期不变时，本国利率相对上升吸引资产购买，本币需求增加，可能升值；风险溢价上升可抵消此效应。\tHypothetical scenario: holding risk and expectations constant, a higher relative home interest rate attracts asset purchases and can appreciate the currency. A rising risk premium may offset this.",
 "利率与汇率关系有条件；投机、通胀预期和资本限制也会改变资金流。\tThe interest-rate link is conditional; speculation, inflation expectations and capital restrictions also affect flows.",
 "其他条件不变，外国更想购买本国资产会怎样？\tOther things equal, what follows greater foreign demand for home assets?", "本币需求右移\tDemand for home currency shifts right", ["本币需求必左移\tCurrency demand must shift left", "进口自动为零\tImports automatically become zero", "汇率必不变\tThe rate cannot change"], ["出口|exports", "资产|assets", "需求|demand"]);
add("exchange-rate-effects", "4.5", "core", "升贬值的经济影响\tEffects of appreciation and depreciation",
 "本币贬值可降低出口外币价格并提高进口本币价格，但净出口、通胀和增长效果取决于弹性、传导与产能。\tDepreciation can lower foreign-currency export prices and raise home-currency import prices, while net exports, inflation and growth depend on elasticities, pass-through and capacity.",
 "本币贬值改变相对价格；出口与进口数量逐步调整；净出口和进口成本共同影响 AD 与 AS\tDepreciation changes relative prices; export and import volumes adjust gradually; net exports and import costs affect AD and AS",
 "原创假设：依赖进口燃料的企业成本上升，可能左移 SRAS；同时出口订单增加可右移 AD，不能只看一个渠道。\tHypothetical scenario: imported fuel becomes dearer, potentially shifting SRAS left, while more export orders may shift AD right. Both channels matter.",
 "贬值不保证贸易余额改善，也可能提高外币债务的本币负担。\tDepreciation does not guarantee a better trade balance and can raise the home-currency burden of foreign-currency debt.",
 "本币贬值对外币债务可能有何影响？\tWhat can depreciation do to foreign-currency debt?", "增加本币偿债负担\tIncrease its home-currency repayment burden", ["自动取消债务\tAutomatically cancel it", "必使进口燃料变便宜\tNecessarily cheapen imported fuel", "必消除通胀\tNecessarily remove inflation"], ["贬值|depreciation", "进口成本|import costs", "弹性|elasticities"], ["16", "16.2", 500]);
add("fixed-exchange-rate", "4.5", "core", "固定汇率与储备干预\tFixed exchange rates and reserve intervention",
 "固定汇率由当局维持目标平价；本币面临贬值压力时，央行可卖外汇储备买本币，但储备有限。\tAuthorities maintain a target parity in a fixed regime. Under downward pressure they can sell foreign reserves and buy home currency, but reserves are finite.",
 "市场汇率低于目标；央行买本币增加需求；外汇储备下降以支持平价\tThe market rate falls below parity; central-bank home-currency purchases add demand; foreign reserves decline to defend the peg",
 "原创假设：目标 1 本币=0.5 美元，市场需求下滑；卖美元买本币可支持目标，持续干预可能需要加息或政策调整。\tHypothetical scenario: the target is 0.5 dollars per home unit and demand falls. Selling dollars to buy home currency supports the target; sustained pressure may require higher rates or policy adjustment.",
 "官方下调固定平价称法定贬值；这不同于浮动市场的贬值。\tAn official reduction of fixed parity is devaluation, distinct from market depreciation.",
 "如何用储备抵抗本币贬值压力？\tHow can reserves resist downward pressure on home currency?", "卖外币买本币\tSell foreign currency and buy home currency", ["卖本币买外币\tSell home currency and buy foreign currency", "完全不交易且保证平价\tNever trade yet guarantee parity", "印本币必提高其价格\tPrint home currency to necessarily raise its price"], ["平价|parity", "储备|reserves", "买本币|buy home currency"], ["16", "16.3", 504]);
add("managed-exchange-rate", "4.5", "core", "管理浮动与制度比较\tManaged floating and regime comparison",
 "管理浮动允许市场决定汇率，同时当局不定期干预；制度选择权衡稳定性、调整能力与政策自主性。\tManaged floating allows market determination with occasional official intervention. Regime choice trades off stability, adjustment and policy autonomy.",
 "市场冲击引起波动；当局选择性干预；汇率风险与政策成本重新分配\tMarket shocks create volatility; authorities intervene selectively; exchange risk and policy costs are redistributed",
 "原创假设：出口集中且资本流动大的经济体希望减少波动，却不能把有限储备当作无限保证；浮动也可能为外部冲击提供缓冲。\tHypothetical scenario: an export-concentrated economy with mobile capital wants less volatility but cannot treat reserves as unlimited. Floating may cushion external shocks.",
 "固定并非永久稳定，浮动也非完全无干预；应说明实际制度与条件。\tFixed does not mean permanently stable, nor floating entirely intervention-free; specify the actual regime and conditions.",
 "管理浮动最符合哪种描述？\tWhich description fits managed floating?", "市场定价加选择性干预\tMarket pricing with selective intervention", ["永远固定同一平价\tAlways one fixed parity", "完全禁止外汇交易\tAll currency trading banned", "自动加入货币联盟\tAutomatic monetary-union membership"], ["市场|market", "干预|intervention", "自主性|autonomy"], ["16", "16.3", 504]);
add("exchange-calculations", "4.5", "hl", "汇率换算与百分比\tCurrency conversion and percentage changes",
 "按报价单位相乘或相除完成换算；百分比变动以初始汇率为分母，倒数报价须重新计算。\tConvert by multiplying or dividing according to units. Percentage changes use the initial rate; inverse quotations need a separate calculation.",
 "写清金额单位；使换算单位约去；用新减旧除以旧计算变动\tWrite amount units; cancel units in conversion; calculate change as new minus old divided by old",
 "原创假设：每美元 8 本币，240 本币可换 30 美元；变为每美元 10 本币，同额只能换 24 美元。本币的美元价值下降 20%，不是 25%。\tHypothetical scenario: at eight home units per dollar, 240 home units buy thirty dollars; at ten, they buy twenty-four. The home currency's dollar value falls 20%, not 25%.",
 "进口账单变化可能还含数量与外币价格变化；应控制条件。\tAn import bill can also change with quantity and foreign price; hold these conditions constant.",
 "每美元 5 本币，100 本币换多少美元？\tAt five home units per dollar, how many dollars do 100 home units buy?", "20 美元\tTwenty dollars", ["500 美元\tFive hundred dollars", "95 美元\tNinety-five dollars", "105 美元\tOne hundred and five dollars"], ["单位|units", "换算|conversion", "初始|initial"]);
add("exchange-policy-trilemma", "4.5", "hl", "汇率制度与政策约束\tExchange regimes and policy constraints",
 "资本自由流动下，固定汇率约束独立货币政策；利差会引发资金流并迫使当局干预或调整政策。\tWith free capital mobility, a fixed exchange rate constrains independent monetary policy: interest differentials trigger flows requiring intervention or policy adjustment.",
 "独立降息降低相对回报；资本流出增加贬值压力；捍卫固定汇率限制降息空间\tIndependent rate cuts reduce relative returns; outflows add depreciation pressure; defending parity restricts rate cuts",
 "原创假设：一国希望降息刺激就业，又维持平价且允许资本自由流动；持续资本外流暴露三目标难以同时保持。\tHypothetical scenario: an economy wants lower rates for jobs, a fixed parity and free capital flows. Persistent outflows expose the difficulty of sustaining all three.",
 "该约束依赖资本流动、风险与可信度，不表示所有国家任何时刻利率完全相同。\tThe constraint depends on mobility, risk and credibility; it does not imply identical interest rates everywhere at every moment.",
 "固定汇率和自由资本流动下，什么受约束？\tWhat is constrained with a fixed rate and free capital flows?", "独立货币政策\tIndependent monetary policy", ["所有国内生产\tAll domestic production", "任何教育支出\tAny education spending", "所有国际贸易\tAll international trade"], ["资本流动|capital mobility", "固定汇率|fixed exchange rate", "货币政策|monetary policy"], ["17", "17.2", 523]);
add("current-account", "4.6", "core", "经常账户的构成\tComponents of the current account",
 "经常账户记录货物、服务、初次收入及二次收入的跨境净流量；贸易余额只是其中一部分。\tThe current account records net cross-border goods, services, primary income and secondary income flows. The trade balance is only part of it.",
 "货物服务出口形成贷项；向国外支付收入形成借项；各项净额相加得到经常账户余额\tGoods and service exports create credits; income paid abroad creates debits; component balances sum to the current account",
 "原创假设：货物 −20、服务 +10、初次收入 −5、二次收入 +3，经常账户为 −12；收到海外亲属汇款通常属二次收入。\tHypothetical scenario: goods −20, services +10, primary income −5 and secondary income +3 give a current-account balance of −12. Family remittances received normally enter secondary income.",
 "海外投资利润属初次收入，购买海外股份属金融账户，不要混淆。\tIncome on foreign investment is primary income; purchasing foreign shares belongs to the financial account.",
 "货物 −10、服务 +4、收入净额 +2，经常账户多少？\tGoods −10, services +4 and combined income +2 give what current balance?", "−4\t−4", ["16\t16", "−16\t−16", "4\t4"], ["货物|goods", "收入|income", "经常账户|current account"]);
add("capital-financial-account", "4.6", "core", "资本账户与金融账户\tCapital and financial accounts",
 "资本账户记录资本转移及非生产非金融资产交易；金融账户记录跨境金融资产与负债交易，包括直接投资、证券投资、其他投资和储备。\tThe capital account records capital transfers and non-produced non-financial assets. The financial account records cross-border asset and liability transactions, including direct, portfolio, other investment and reserves.",
 "跨境融资改变资产负债；按投资性质分类；与经常项目形成对应记录\tCross-border finance changes assets and liabilities; classify the type of investment; record counterparts to current transactions",
 "原创假设：外国企业建厂属直接投资，居民买外国债券属证券投资；贷款本金偿还是金融交易，利息是初次收入。\tHypothetical scenario: a foreign firm building a factory is direct investment and residents buying foreign bonds is portfolio investment. Loan principal repayment is financial, while interest is primary income.",
 "日常所说资本流入大多属于金融账户，不应把资本账户当作所有投资的总称。\tMost everyday capital inflows belong to the financial account; the capital account is not a catch-all for investment.",
 "偿还海外贷款本金记在哪里？\tWhere is foreign loan principal repayment recorded?", "金融账户\tThe financial account", ["货物出口\tGoods exports", "二次收入\tSecondary income", "国内消费 CPI\tDomestic consumption CPI"], ["资产|assets", "负债|liabilities", "金融账户|financial account"]);
add("bop-identity", "4.6", "hl", "国际收支恒等式与符号\tBalance-of-payments identity and signs",
 "采用金融账户为净资本流入的教学符号时，CA+KA+FA+误差遗漏=0；官方净资产获得减负债增加的符号则相反。\tWith a teaching convention that defines FA as net financial inflows, CA+KA+FA+errors=0. The official net-acquisition-of-assets-minus-liabilities convention uses the opposite FA sign.",
 "声明金融账户符号；记录交易对应项；用误差遗漏协调统计差异\tState the financial-account sign convention; record transaction counterparts; use errors and omissions for statistical discrepancies",
 "原创假设：CA=−30、KA=0、误差=0，则教学净流入 FA=+30；官方净借出符号下 FA=−30。储备交易已经包含在金融账户中。\tHypothetical scenario: CA=−30, KA=0 and no errors imply teaching-convention inflows FA=+30, or official net-lending FA=−30. Reserve transactions are already within the financial account.",
 "不要既把储备计入金融账户又另加一次；国际收支平衡不等于经常账户余额为零。\tDo not count reserves inside FA and then add them again; balanced accounts do not imply a zero current account.",
 "净流入符号下 CA=−12、KA=0、无误差，FA 为多少？\tUsing net inflows, CA=−12, KA=0 and no errors imply what FA?", "+12\t+12", ["−12\t−12", "0\t0", "必须再重复加储备\tReserves must be added again"], ["符号|convention", "对应|counterparts", "储备|reserves"], ["17", "17.1", 520]);
add("current-account-imbalances", "4.6", "core", "经常账户失衡的原因与可持续性\tCauses and sustainability of current-account imbalances",
 "经常账户逆差可能反映投资进口、竞争力不足或内需强劲；其可持续性取决于融资结构、偿债能力与资金用途。\tA current deficit may reflect investment imports, weak competitiveness or strong domestic demand. Sustainability depends on financing structure, repayment capacity and how funds are used.",
 "进口或收入支付超过相应收入；外部融资或储备变化对应缺口；未来收益与融资稳定性决定风险\tImports or income payments exceed receipts; external financing or reserves correspond to the gap; future returns and financing stability determine risks",
 "原创假设：设备进口支持未来出口，与短期外币借款资助消费具有不同风险；长期直接投资通常比易撤出的短期融资更稳定。\tHypothetical scenario: machinery imports supporting future exports differ from short-term foreign-currency borrowing funding consumption. Long-term direct investment is generally more stable than easily reversed short-term finance.",
 "逆差不必然坏，顺差也可能反映内需不足；应比较规模、期限、币种与结构。\tDeficits are not automatically bad, nor surpluses always good; compare size, maturity, currency and structure.",
 "哪种情况通常增加逆差融资脆弱性？\tWhat normally increases deficit-financing vulnerability?", "短期外币债务依赖\tDependence on short-term foreign-currency debt", ["高回报生产性投资本身\tProductive high-return investment alone", "期限延长本身\tLonger maturity alone", "出口多样化本身\tExport diversification alone"], ["融资|financing", "可持续性|sustainability", "债务|debt"], ["17", "17.4", 530]);
add("marshall-lerner", "4.6", "hl", "马歇尔—勒纳条件\tThe Marshall–Lerner condition",
 "在初始贸易平衡等标准假设下，贬值改善贸易余额要求出口与进口需求价格弹性的绝对值之和大于 1。\tUnder standard assumptions including initial trade balance, depreciation improves the trade balance when absolute export and import demand elasticities sum to more than one.",
 "贬值改变相对价格；数量按需求弹性调整；数量效应超过进口单位成本效应时余额改善\tDepreciation changes relative prices; volumes respond to demand elasticities; the balance improves when volume effects outweigh the import unit-cost effect",
 "原创假设：出口弹性 0.7、进口弹性 0.6，总和 1.3，在充分供给反应和相关模型假设下支持改善；不意味着一定立即改善。\tHypothetical scenario: elasticities 0.7 and 0.6 sum to 1.3, supporting improvement with sufficient supply response and the model's assumptions; improvement need not be immediate.",
 "条件针对贸易余额，不自动覆盖投资收益和转移；弹性不是百分比数量变化本身。\tThe condition concerns the trade balance, not all income and transfers; an elasticity is not the quantity percentage change itself.",
 "哪组弹性满足标准条件？\tWhich elasticity pair satisfies the standard condition?", "0.7 与 0.6\t0.7 and 0.6", ["0.2 与 0.3\t0.2 and 0.3", "0.4 与 0.4\t0.4 and 0.4", "0.1 与 0.2\t0.1 and 0.2"], ["贬值|depreciation", "弹性|elasticities", "大于1|greater than one"], ["17", "17.4", 530]);
add("j-curve", "4.6", "hl", "J 曲线与调整时滞\tThe J-curve and adjustment lags",
 "贬值后贸易余额可能先恶化后改善，因为合同与消费习惯使数量反应滞后于进口价格变化。\tAfter depreciation the trade balance may first worsen and later improve because contracts and habits delay quantity responses relative to import-price changes.",
 "进口本币单价先上升；短期合同使数量调整缓慢；长期弹性增大可能改善余额\tHome-currency import prices rise first; contracts slow initial volume adjustment; higher long-run elasticities may improve the balance",
 "原创假设：进口燃料合同量短期固定，贬值先增加账单；之后企业节能并改用本地投入，进口量才下降。\tHypothetical scenario: contracted fuel volumes initially remain fixed, so depreciation raises the bill first. Firms later conserve energy and substitute domestic inputs, reducing imports.",
 "J 形只是可能路径；若长期弹性不足或供给受限，余额可能始终不改善。\tThe J shape is only a possible path; weak long-run elasticities or supply constraints can prevent improvement.",
 "J 曲线初期恶化主要反映什么？\tWhat chiefly explains initial J-curve deterioration?", "数量调整慢于价格\tQuantities adjust more slowly than prices", ["出口永远消失\tExports vanish forever", "进口单价必下降\tImport unit prices must fall", "弹性总等于零\tElasticities are always zero"], ["合同|contracts", "时滞|lags", "数量|volumes"], ["17", "17.4", 530]);
add("imbalance-policies", "4.6", "hl", "支出转换、支出减少与供给侧措施\tExpenditure switching, reduction and supply policies",
 "经常账户政策可转换支出来源、减少总支出或改善供给竞争力，各有时滞和宏观目标代价。\tCurrent-account policies can switch spending sources, reduce total expenditure or improve supply competitiveness, each with lags and macroeconomic trade-offs.",
 "转换政策改变相对价格；紧缩减少进口需求；生产率政策改善长期竞争力\tSwitching policies alter relative prices; contraction reduces import demand; productivity policy improves long-run competitiveness",
 "原创假设：加息压低消费和进口可能缩小逆差，却增加失业且可能吸引资本升值；培训与物流改善较慢但可提高出口能力。\tHypothetical scenario: higher rates may cut consumption and imports but raise unemployment and attract appreciating capital flows. Training and logistics take longer but can improve export capacity.",
 "不能忽略汇率的反向渠道，也不能把需求压缩导致的逆差改善当作无成本成功。\tDo not omit the exchange-rate counterchannel or treat deficit reduction through demand compression as costless.",
 "哪项属于长期供给改善？\tWhich is a long-run supply improvement?", "提高技能和物流效率\tImproving skills and logistics", ["只减少消费\tOnly reducing consumption", "直接配给所有进口\tDirectly rationing every import", "仅改变记账符号\tOnly changing accounting signs"], ["转换|switching", "紧缩|contraction", "生产率|productivity"], ["17", "17.4", 530]);
add("sustainable-development", "4.7", "core", "增长、发展与可持续性\tGrowth, development and sustainability",
 "经济发展涵盖健康、教育、机会和生活质量；可持续发展要求满足当前需要而不损害后代满足需要的能力。\tDevelopment concerns health, education, opportunity and quality of life. Sustainable development meets present needs without compromising future generations' ability to meet theirs.",
 "产出增长扩大可用资源；分配与公共服务影响能力；自然资本保护维持未来选择\tOutput growth expands available resources; distribution and public services shape capabilities; natural-capital protection preserves future options",
 "原创假设：采矿提高 GDP，但污染水源并挤压农业，不能只用产出增长判断发展；需衡量健康、收入分配和生态损失。\tHypothetical scenario: mining raises GDP but pollutes water and harms farming. Evaluate health, distribution and ecological losses alongside output.",
 "增长可能资助发展，但并非充分条件；可持续性也包含代际公平。\tGrowth can finance development but is not sufficient; sustainability includes intergenerational equity.",
 "GDP 增长但水源污染扩大，应补充衡量什么？\tIf GDP rises while water pollution worsens, what else should be measured?", "健康与自然资本损失\tHealth and natural-capital losses", ["只看 GDP 总量\tOnly total GDP", "只看出口收入\tOnly export receipts", "不需考虑未来\tNo need to consider the future"], ["发展|development", "自然资本|natural capital", "后代|future generations"]);
add("environment-poverty", "4.7", "core", "贫困、环境与共同资源\tPoverty, environment and common resources",
 "贫困可能迫使家庭依赖短期资源开采，环境退化又削弱生计；产权、替代收入和公共服务影响这一循环。\tPoverty can push households toward short-run resource extraction, while degradation undermines livelihoods. Property rights, alternative incomes and public services influence the cycle.",
 "低收入限制替代选择；过度使用共同资源；资源退化使收入更脆弱\tLow income restricts alternatives; common resources are overused; degradation makes income more vulnerable",
 "原创假设：缺乏可靠电力的村庄依赖薪柴，单独禁伐可能伤害穷人；社区管理与清洁能源可同时改善激励和选择。\tHypothetical scenario: a village without reliable power relies on fuelwood. A logging ban alone may harm poor households; community management and clean energy improve incentives and alternatives together.",
 "环境破坏也可能来自富裕群体的高消费；不能把责任全部归于穷人。\tHigh consumption among wealthy groups can also damage the environment; responsibility cannot be assigned solely to poor people.",
 "什么最可能兼顾生计和资源保护？\tWhat can best support livelihoods and conservation together?", "替代能源加社区管理\tAlternative energy plus community management", ["无补偿全面禁用\tA blanket ban without support", "放任无限开采\tUnlimited unregulated extraction", "忽略资源产权\tIgnoring resource rights"], ["贫困|poverty", "资源|resources", "生计|livelihoods"]);
add("sdg-policy", "4.7", "core", "可持续发展目标与政策权衡\tSustainable development goals and policy trade-offs",
 "发展政策需要同时评价减贫、健康、教育、环境和制度目标，用明确指标检验协同与冲突。\tDevelopment policy should evaluate poverty, health, education, environment and institutions together, using explicit indicators to test synergies and conflicts.",
 "确定具体目标与基线；识别协同及机会成本；用分组指标追踪结果\tSet specific goals and baselines; identify synergies and opportunity costs; track outcomes with disaggregated indicators",
 "原创假设：清洁公交可减少污染并改善就业可达性，但票价上涨可能排斥低收入者；比较定向补助与财政成本。\tHypothetical scenario: clean buses reduce pollution and improve job access, but higher fares may exclude low-income riders. Compare targeted support with fiscal costs.",
 "宣布目标不等于观察到进展；要注明指标、年份和群体。\tAnnouncing a goal is not observing progress; specify indicators, years and groups.",
 "判断项目是否促进发展最需要什么？\tWhat is most needed to judge a project's development effect?", "有基线的多维结果指标\tMultidimensional outcomes with a baseline", ["只有项目名称\tOnly the project name", "只统计宣传数量\tOnly publicity counts", "只看支出越多越好\tAssume more spending is always better"], ["目标|goals", "指标|indicators", "权衡|trade-offs"]);
add("development-indicators", "4.8", "core", "人均收入与 PPP 比较\tIncome per capita and PPP comparison",
 "人均 GNI 衡量平均居民收入，PPP 调整价格水平差异；两者都不能充分揭示分配、公共服务或环境质量。\tGNI per capita measures average resident income; PPP adjusts for price-level differences. Neither fully captures distribution, public services or environmental quality.",
 "总收入除以人口；按购买力调整跨国可比性；用其他指标补充平均数局限\tDivide total income by population; adjust purchasing power for cross-country comparison; add indicators to address average-income limits",
 "原创假设：A 与 B 汇率换算收入相同，但 A 的基本生活篮子更便宜，PPP 比较可能显示 A 购买力更高；仍需看地区差距。\tHypothetical scenario: A and B have equal exchange-rate-converted income, but basic goods are cheaper in A. PPP may show greater purchasing power in A; regional inequality still matters.",
 "PPP 不是外汇市场可交易的汇率，人均收入也不是典型家庭的实际收入。\tPPP is not a tradable market exchange rate; average income is not necessarily a typical household's income.",
 "PPP 调整主要解决什么问题？\tWhat does PPP adjustment chiefly address?", "跨国价格水平差异\tCross-country price-level differences", ["自动消除不平等\tAutomatically eliminating inequality", "使所有寿命相等\tEqualising all lifespans", "衡量全部污染\tMeasuring all pollution"], ["人均|per capita", "价格水平|price levels", "购买力|purchasing power"]);
add("hdi", "4.8", "core", "人类发展指数\tThe Human Development Index",
 "HDI 综合健康、教育与生活水平，使用预期寿命、预期和平均受教育年限、PPP 人均 GNI，并以几何平均组合维度指数。\tHDI combines health, education and living standards using life expectancy, expected and mean schooling years, and PPP GNI per capita, with a geometric mean of dimension indices.",
 "将各维度标准化；教育指标组成教育维度；几何平均限制单一高维度完全补偿低维度\tNormalise dimensions; combine schooling indicators into education; the geometric mean limits full compensation of a weak dimension by a strong one",
 "原创假设：甲乙收入类似，甲的寿命与教育更高，HDI 可能更高；但国平均仍掩盖性别与地区差距。\tHypothetical scenario: two economies have similar income but one has better longevity and education, potentially giving it higher HDI. National averages still hide gender and regional gaps.",
 "HDI 不是三个原始单位直接相加，也不是完整的生态或政治自由指标。\tHDI does not add raw units directly and is not a comprehensive ecological or political-freedom measure.",
 "哪个属于 HDI 的健康指标？\tWhich is HDI's health indicator?", "出生时预期寿命\tLife expectancy at birth", ["货物出口\tGoods exports", "汇率波动\tExchange-rate volatility", "关税收入\tTariff revenue"], ["健康|health", "教育|education", "收入|income"]);
add("multidimensional-poverty", "4.8", "core", "多维贫困与不平等调整\tMultidimensional poverty and inequality adjustment",
 "多维贫困指标结合健康、教育和生活条件的重叠剥夺；不平等调整的 HDI 则反映各维度分配差异。\tMultidimensional poverty measures overlapping deprivations in health, education and living conditions; inequality-adjusted HDI reflects distribution within dimensions.",
 "识别家庭剥夺；按明确权重和阈值分类；结合发生率与强度判断贫困\tIdentify household deprivations; classify using explicit weights and thresholds; combine incidence and intensity to assess poverty",
 "原创假设：收入略高于贫困线的家庭仍可能缺安全饮水和教育；只用收入会漏掉这些剥夺。指标权重会影响排名。\tHypothetical scenario: a household just above an income poverty line may still lack safe water and schooling. Income alone misses these deprivations, while indicator weights affect rankings.",
 "不同指标回答不同问题，不能把多维贫困率、Gini 与 HDI 当成同一种量。\tDifferent indicators answer different questions; multidimensional poverty, Gini and HDI are not interchangeable.",
 "为何要补充多维贫困指标？\tWhy add multidimensional poverty indicators?", "收入未显示所有基本服务剥夺\tIncome misses some basic-service deprivations", ["收入完全无用\tIncome is entirely useless", "所有权重天然唯一\tWeights are uniquely predetermined", "可以不采集数据\tNo data collection is needed"], ["剥夺|deprivations", "发生率|incidence", "强度|intensity"]);
add("measurement-limits", "4.8", "core", "发展数据的可比性与局限\tComparability and limits of development data",
 "发展比较应使用可比年份、定义和人口组，注意非正规经济、统计能力、均值掩盖差异与相关不等于因果。\tDevelopment comparisons need comparable years, definitions and population groups, with attention to informality, statistical capacity, hidden disparities and correlation versus causation.",
 "检查来源和定义；统一年份与可比单位；结合定量指标和情境解释\tCheck sources and definitions; align years and comparable units; combine quantitative measures with context",
 "原创假设：农村调查遗漏偏远家庭，可能高估全国服务覆盖；比较政策前后还需考虑经济周期和其他政策。\tHypothetical scenario: omitting remote households can overstate national service coverage. Before-after policy comparisons also need business-cycle and other-policy context.",
 "两个指标同时改善不能单独证明某政策造成改善；缺失数据不等于零。\tTwo improving indicators alone do not prove a policy caused improvement; missing data are not zero.",
 "某地区没有卫生数据应如何处理？\tHow should missing health data for a region be handled?", "标明缺失并限制结论\tMark it missing and limit conclusions", ["填为零并排名\tInsert zero and rank", "默认全国平均完全适用\tAssume the national mean applies exactly", "宣称没有健康问题\tDeclare no health problems"], ["可比|comparable", "数据|data", "局限|limits"]);
add("poverty-cycle", "4.9", "core", "贫困循环与资本形成\tPoverty cycles and capital formation",
 "低收入可能导致低储蓄、低投资与低生产率，进而维持低收入；这是一种可能自我强化的机制而非不可改变的命运。\tLow income can limit saving and investment, keeping productivity and income low. This is a potentially reinforcing mechanism, not an inevitable destiny.",
 "低收入限制储蓄；资金不足抑制资本形成；低生产率维持低收入\tLow income restricts saving; limited finance constrains capital formation; low productivity sustains low income",
 "原创假设：农户无法承担灌溉投资，旱季低产又使下年投资更难；公共灌溉、风险保险或适当融资可打断循环。\tHypothetical scenario: a farmer cannot finance irrigation, and low dry-season yields reduce next year's investment capacity. Public irrigation, insurance or suitable finance can interrupt the cycle.",
 "低储蓄只是障碍之一；信贷不能替代可靠项目、产权和市场需求。\tLow saving is only one barrier; credit cannot substitute for viable projects, rights and demand.",
 "哪条链说明贫困循环？\tWhich chain illustrates a poverty cycle?", "低收入→低投资→低生产率\tLow income → low investment → low productivity", ["高收入必致低寿命\tHigh income must lower longevity", "贷款总能消除贫困\tLoans always remove poverty", "储蓄必直接消失\tSaving must vanish"], ["收入|income", "投资|investment", "生产率|productivity"], ["19", "19.1", 564]);
add("human-capital-infrastructure", "4.9", "core", "人力资本与基础设施不足\tHuman-capital and infrastructure gaps",
 "健康、教育、电力、交通和数字基础设施不足可提高成本、限制生产率并阻碍进入市场。\tGaps in health, education, electricity, transport and digital infrastructure can raise costs, restrict productivity and limit market access.",
 "服务缺口限制能力；停电和运输延误提高成本；低回报抑制投资与就业\tService gaps restrict capabilities; outages and transport delays raise costs; weak returns discourage investment and jobs",
 "原创假设：学校扩招但学生因疾病缺勤、企业因停电停工，单独增加学位未必转化为生产率；需要互补投入。\tHypothetical scenario: schooling expands but illness causes absence and outages halt firms. More school places alone may not raise productivity without complementary investments.",
 "建设数量不等于服务质量；维护、师资和可负担性影响真实覆盖。\tConstruction counts do not establish service quality; maintenance, teachers and affordability determine effective access.",
 "为什么道路建设后仍应观察运输服务？\tWhy assess transport services after road construction?", "维护与使用条件决定实际收益\tMaintenance and access determine actual benefits", ["建设支出就是最终福利\tConstruction spending is final welfare", "所有地区必同等受益\tEvery region must gain equally", "不再需测量结果\tOutcomes need no measurement"], ["健康|health", "基础设施|infrastructure", "成本|costs"]);
add("primary-dependence", "4.9", "core", "初级产品依赖与贸易条件\tPrimary-product dependence and terms of trade",
 "出口集中于少数初级产品会增加收入波动；贸易条件指数=出口价格指数÷进口价格指数×100，恶化意味着每单位出口能换更少进口。\tConcentration in primary exports increases revenue risk. Terms of trade equal the export price index divided by the import price index times 100; deterioration means fewer imports per export unit.",
 "出口集中放大外部价格冲击；外汇和税收波动；资本品进口与公共投资受限\tExport concentration magnifies world-price shocks; foreign exchange and tax revenue fluctuate; capital-goods imports and public investment are constrained",
 "原创假设：出口价指数 90、进口价指数 120，贸易条件为 75。收入还取决于出口数量，不能仅从价格比率推断贸易余额。\tHypothetical scenario: export prices indexed at ninety and imports at 120 give terms of trade of 75. Revenue also depends on volume, so the ratio alone cannot establish the trade balance.",
 "贸易条件不是汇率，也不是出口总额除以进口总额；长期价格下降并非每种商品必然发生。\tTerms of trade are neither an exchange rate nor total export receipts divided by imports; long-run deterioration is not inevitable for every commodity.",
 "出口价指数 110、进口价指数 100，贸易条件多少？\tExport price index 110 and import price index 100 give what terms of trade?", "110\t110", ["90.9\t90.9", "10\t10", "210\t210"], ["出口价格|export prices", "进口价格|import prices", "波动|volatility"]);
add("debt-finance-barriers", "4.9", "core", "债务、金融排斥与资本外逃\tDebt, financial exclusion and capital flight",
 "高偿债负担可挤压公共投资；缺少抵押、保险和支付服务限制家庭企业投资；资本外逃削弱国内融资。\tHeavy debt service can crowd out public investment; missing collateral, insurance and payments constrain private investment, while capital flight weakens domestic finance.",
 "融资约束限制项目；外币债务暴露汇率风险；偿债挤压健康教育预算\tFinance constraints restrict projects; foreign-currency debt exposes exchange risk; debt service squeezes health and education budgets",
 "原创假设：政府外币债务本息不变，本币贬值后本币税收需覆盖更多偿付；债务重组可缓解但涉及债权人协调与未来融资。\tHypothetical scenario: unchanged foreign-currency debt service requires more home-currency tax revenue after depreciation. Restructuring may help but involves creditor coordination and future borrowing access.",
 "借债并非必然有害；应比较投资回报、利率、期限、币种和偿付能力。\tBorrowing is not inherently harmful; compare returns, rates, maturity, currency and repayment capacity.",
 "何种组合最增加偿债脆弱性？\tWhich combination most increases debt vulnerability?", "外币债务高且本币贬值\tHigh foreign-currency debt and home depreciation", ["币种匹配改善\tImproved currency matching", "投资回报提高\tHigher investment returns", "期限风险降低\tLower maturity risk"], ["融资|finance", "债务|debt", "偿债|debt service"]);
add("institutions-barriers", "4.9", "core", "制度、冲突与社会排斥\tInstitutions, conflict and social exclusion",
 "腐败、产权不清、冲突和歧视可增加交易风险、降低投资并限制人们参与教育和就业。\tCorruption, insecure rights, conflict and discrimination can raise transaction risk, discourage investment and restrict access to education and jobs.",
 "规则不透明增加不确定性；排斥限制人才配置；低投资与低信任阻碍发展\tOpaque rules increase uncertainty; exclusion misallocates talent; weak investment and trust obstruct development",
 "原创假设：女性难以持有土地或取得贷款，使高回报项目无法融资；法律改革还需执行、信息和安全保障。\tHypothetical scenario: women unable to own land or obtain credit cannot finance high-return projects. Legal reform also needs enforcement, information and safety.",
 "制度不能只用一个排名解释；改革效果取决于历史、执行能力与当地参与。\tA single ranking cannot explain institutions; reform depends on history, implementation capacity and local participation.",
 "产权改革促进投资还需要什么？\tWhat else is needed for property-rights reform to support investment?", "可信执行与可获得的司法\tCredible enforcement and accessible justice", ["只有书面法律即可\tWritten law alone suffices", "完全忽略弱势群体\tIgnore excluded groups", "无需市场需求\tNo market demand"], ["规则|rules", "排斥|exclusion", "投资|investment"], ["19", "19.3", 581]);
add("geography-informality", "4.9", "core", "地理、非正规经济与多重障碍\tGeography, informality and interacting barriers",
 "内陆位置、气候风险和市场距离可能提高成本；非正规就业可提供生计，却常缺社会保障、融资和统计覆盖。\tLandlocked locations, climate risks and distance can raise costs. Informal work provides livelihoods but often lacks protection, finance and statistical coverage.",
 "距离与风险提高交易成本；企业留在小规模非正规经营；税基与公共服务能力受限\tDistance and risk raise transaction costs; firms remain small and informal; the tax base and public-service capacity are constrained",
 "原创假设：内陆农户同时面临差路、洪灾和无保险，仅取消营业许可费未必解决主要瓶颈；需识别互补约束。\tHypothetical scenario: landlocked farmers face poor roads, floods and no insurance. Removing licence fees alone may not address binding constraints; identify complementary barriers.",
 "地理不等于命运，非正规活动也不都非法；政策应降低正规化成本并提供实际收益。\tGeography is not destiny, and informal activity is not all illegal; formalisation should reduce costs and offer real benefits.",
 "多重障碍同时存在时应怎样选政策？\tHow should policies be chosen with interacting barriers?", "识别主要瓶颈和互补投入\tIdentify binding constraints and complementary inputs", ["假设一个措施必解决全部\tAssume one measure solves everything", "只处罚所有小商贩\tOnly penalise every small trader", "认定地理无法改变任何结果\tAssume geography prevents any improvement"], ["成本|costs", "非正规|informal", "约束|constraints"]);
add("trade-strategies", "4.10", "core", "进口替代与出口导向\tImport substitution and export promotion",
 "进口替代扶持本地生产替代进口；出口导向帮助企业进入国际市场，两者的成效取决于竞争、学习和政策纪律。\tImport substitution supports domestic production replacing imports; export promotion helps firms reach world markets. Outcomes depend on competition, learning and policy discipline.",
 "选择产业与政策工具；市场与学习激励影响成本；出口收入或进口节约支持资本品需求\tChoose sectors and instruments; market and learning incentives affect costs; export earnings or import savings support capital imports",
 "原创假设：关税扶持小市场汽车业可能限制规模；出口支持若要求绩效并改善物流，可保留竞争压力，但也暴露于外需波动。\tHypothetical scenario: tariff-supported car production in a small market may lack scale. Export support tied to performance and logistics can preserve competition but exposes firms to world-demand volatility.",
 "两者不是只能二选一的标签；具体工具、退出机制与产业条件更重要。\tThese are not mutually exclusive labels; instruments, exit rules and sector conditions matter.",
 "哪项能降低进口替代的长期低效风险？\tWhat can reduce long-run inefficiency under import substitution?", "绩效条件和明确退出机制\tPerformance conditions and a credible exit", ["永久无条件保护\tPermanent unconditional protection", "禁止所有技术进口\tBan all technology imports", "不衡量成本\tNever measure costs"], ["进口替代|import substitution", "出口|exports", "竞争|competition"]);
add("diversification-enterprise", "4.10", "core", "多样化与社会企业\tDiversification and social enterprise",
 "产业和出口多样化减少对单一收入来源的依赖；社会企业以商业活动支持社会目标，但仍面临成本和治理约束。\tDiversification reduces reliance on a single income source. Social enterprises use business activity to pursue social goals but still face cost and governance constraints.",
 "开发不同市场和产品；降低高度相关的收入风险；技能和融资支持新活动\tDevelop different products and markets; reduce highly correlated revenue risks; skills and finance support new activities",
 "原创假设：咖啡合作社增加加工和生态旅游，可能提高附加值并分散风险；若两者都依赖同一气候或游客市场，风险分散有限。\tHypothetical scenario: a coffee cooperative adds processing and ecotourism, potentially adding value and spreading risk. Diversification is limited if both remain exposed to the same climate or visitor market.",
 "项目数量增加不一定分散风险；社会目标也不保证经营或影响有效。\tMore projects do not necessarily diversify risk; social intent does not guarantee operational or impact success.",
 "何种多样化更能降低风险？\tWhat diversification most reduces risk?", "收入来源受不同冲击影响\tIncome sources exposed to different shocks", ["仅更改同一商品名称\tOnly renaming the same commodity", "所有活动依赖同一买家\tEvery activity depends on one buyer", "完全不看需求\tIgnore demand entirely"], ["多样化|diversification", "风险|risk", "社会目标|social goals"], ["20", "20.2", 599]);
add("market-based-development", "4.10", "core", "市场导向的发展政策\tMarket-based development policies",
 "自由化、私有化和放松不必要监管可增强竞争与激励，但需要竞争政策、公共利益保护和可执行制度。\tLiberalisation, privatisation and removal of unnecessary regulation may improve competition and incentives, supported by competition policy, public-interest safeguards and effective institutions.",
 "降低进入障碍；竞争与产权激励改善效率；监管处理垄断与外部性\tLower entry barriers; competition and ownership incentives improve efficiency; regulation addresses monopoly and externalities",
 "原创假设：出售国有供水企业若不设置价格和质量监管，可能仅把公共垄断变为私人垄断；结果要看覆盖、质量和价格。\tHypothetical scenario: selling a public water supplier without price or quality regulation may merely create a private monopoly. Assess coverage, quality and prices.",
 "私有化不是竞争的同义词；一次出售收入也不是持续财政改善的充分证据。\tPrivatisation is not synonymous with competition; one-off sale revenue does not prove lasting fiscal improvement.",
 "自然垄断私有化应重点配合什么？\tWhat particularly needs to accompany natural-monopoly privatisation?", "价格质量监管与问责\tPrice-quality regulation and accountability", ["自动取消所有监管\tAutomatically remove all regulation", "保证企业无成本\tGuarantee zero costs", "只比较出售当天收入\tOnly compare sale-day revenue"], ["竞争|competition", "激励|incentives", "监管|regulation"], ["20", "20.3", 602]);
add("public-services-development", "4.10", "core", "公共服务、再分配与发展\tPublic services, redistribution and development",
 "教育、健康、基础设施和定向转移可改善能力与机会，但财政空间、服务质量和执行决定结果。\tEducation, health, infrastructure and targeted transfers can improve capabilities and opportunities; fiscal space, service quality and implementation determine outcomes.",
 "公共服务降低个人进入障碍；健康技能提高参与和生产率；公平与增长可能相互促进\tServices lower individual barriers; health and skills improve participation and productivity; equity and growth may reinforce each other",
 "原创假设：儿童现金补助配合附近有质量的学校，可能改善出勤；若学校缺师资，仅要求出勤会增加家庭负担。\tHypothetical scenario: child transfers combined with accessible quality schools may improve attendance. Requiring attendance where teachers are absent can burden families.",
 "政府支出不是自动有效，必须比较机会成本、漏损和受益群体。\tPublic spending is not automatically effective; assess opportunity cost, leakage and beneficiaries.",
 "评估教育支出应看什么？\tWhat should be assessed for education spending?", "学习成果、覆盖和机会成本\tLearning outcomes, access and opportunity cost", ["只看预算增加\tOnly budget increases", "不看服务质量\tIgnore service quality", "只统计建筑面积\tOnly floor area"], ["服务|services", "能力|capabilities", "质量|quality"], ["20", "20.4", 606]);
add("fdi-mncs", "4.10", "core", "外国直接投资与跨国公司\tForeign direct investment and multinational firms",
 "FDI 可带来资本、就业、技术和出口联系，也可能伴随利润汇出、市场势力、环境成本与有限本地联系。\tFDI can bring capital, jobs, technology and export linkages, alongside profit repatriation, market power, environmental costs and weak local linkages.",
 "跨国企业投入资本技术；雇佣与采购产生本地联系；制度与吸收能力影响技术溢出\tMultinationals bring capital and technology; hiring and procurement create local linkages; institutions and absorptive capacity shape spillovers",
 "原创假设：外资厂培训本地员工并采购本地零件，可扩散技能；若全部进口投入并获长期免税，本地净收益可能较小。\tHypothetical scenario: training local staff and buying local parts can spread skills. Importing all inputs with prolonged tax holidays may leave smaller local net gains.",
 "FDI 流入不等于当年经常账户收入；后续利润汇出通常影响初次收入。\tFDI inflow is not current-account income; later repatriated profits normally affect primary income.",
 "哪项最可能增强 FDI 的本地技术收益？\tWhat most supports local technology gains from FDI?", "员工培训与本地供应商联系\tStaff training and local supplier linkages", ["完全隔离本地企业\tComplete isolation from local firms", "无条件永久免税\tUnconditional permanent tax exemption", "只统计流入金额\tOnly count inflow value"], ["资本|capital", "技术|technology", "联系|linkages"], ["20", "20.5", 611]);
add("aid-ngos", "4.10", "core", "援助、非政府组织与本地参与\tAid, NGOs and local participation",
 "人道援助应对紧急需要，发展援助支持长期能力；赠款、贷款及附带条件的援助对受援者影响不同。\tHumanitarian aid addresses emergencies, while development aid supports long-term capabilities. Grants, loans and tied aid have different effects on recipients.",
 "外部资源缓解约束；项目设计影响本地所有权；问责与评估决定持续效果\tExternal resources relax constraints; project design shapes local ownership; accountability and evaluation determine lasting effects",
 "原创假设：灾后供水赠款能救急；若只采购捐助国昂贵设备且无本地维修培训，长期效果可能有限。NGO 也需协调和问责。\tHypothetical scenario: emergency water grants help after disaster, but expensive donor-country equipment without local repair training may not last. NGOs also need coordination and accountability.",
 "援助不都是免费资金；贷款增加偿还义务，附带采购条件可能提高成本。\tAid is not all free money; loans create repayment obligations and tied procurement may raise costs.",
 "什么最可能提高供水援助的持续性？\tWhat most improves the durability of water aid?", "本地维修能力和参与\tLocal repair capacity and participation", ["只举行交付仪式\tOnly a handover ceremony", "不提供维护经费\tNo maintenance funding", "不问居民需求\tNo assessment of residents' needs"], ["援助|aid", "能力|capacity", "问责|accountability"], ["20", "20.6", 615]);
add("multilateral-debt-relief", "4.10", "core", "多边机构与债务减免\tMultilateral institutions and debt relief",
 "多边发展融资可支持长期项目，国际收支支持可缓解外部融资压力；贷款条件和债务减免需评价财政空间与社会代价。\tMultilateral development finance can support long-term projects, while balance-of-payments support eases external financing pressure. Conditions and debt relief require evaluation of fiscal space and social costs.",
 "外部融资缓解短缺；条件改变政策路径；债务重组或减免影响未来支出与融资激励\tExternal finance eases shortages; conditions alter policy paths; restructuring or relief affects future spending and financing incentives",
 "原创假设：债务减免释放卫生预算，但若治理和税基问题未变，新债仍可能累积；紧缩条件也需保护基本服务。\tHypothetical scenario: debt relief frees health spending, but new debt can build up if governance and revenue problems remain. Fiscal conditions also need protection for essential services.",
 "不能把 IMF、世界银行和 WTO 当作同一机构；项目条款与现行职责须查原始资料。\tThe IMF, World Bank and WTO are distinct institutions; project terms and current mandates require primary-source checks.",
 "债务减免的一个可能发展收益是什么？\tWhat is one potential development gain from debt relief?", "释放基本服务的财政空间\tFreeing fiscal space for essential services", ["永久消除一切融资约束\tPermanently removing all financing constraints", "保证没有治理问题\tGuaranteeing no governance problems", "自动使所有进口免费\tAutomatically making all imports free"], ["融资|finance", "条件|conditions", "财政空间|fiscal space"], ["20", "20.7", 623]);
add("institutional-change", "4.10", "core", "制度改革、包容性金融与赋权\tInstitutional reform, inclusive finance and empowerment",
 "可信法治、透明预算、可获得的金融服务和性别平等可改善参与和投资，但改革需结合当地执行能力。\tCredible rule of law, transparent budgets, accessible finance and gender equality can improve participation and investment, with reforms adapted to local implementation capacity.",
 "规则与信息改善降低风险；弱势群体获得融资和机会；监督与执行维持信任\tBetter rules and information reduce risk; excluded groups gain finance and opportunities; oversight and enforcement maintain trust",
 "原创假设：小额贷款配合储蓄、保险和培训可帮助经营；对无稳定现金流的家庭高息放贷可能加重负担，不能假设借款即脱贫。\tHypothetical scenario: microcredit combined with saving, insurance and training may support enterprise. High-interest lending to households without stable cash flow can worsen burdens; borrowing does not itself establish poverty reduction.",
 "数字账户数量不等于有效金融包容；费用、识字、安全和实际使用同样关键。\tAccount counts do not establish effective inclusion; fees, literacy, safety and actual use matter.",
 "评估小额信贷最应看哪项？\tWhat most matters when evaluating microcredit?", "净收入、还款压力与实际用途\tNet income, repayment stress and actual use", ["只看发放笔数\tOnly number of loans", "贷款越大必越好\tLarger loans are always better", "不看利率与风险\tIgnore rates and risks"], ["规则|rules", "融资|finance", "参与|participation"], ["20", "20.8", 627]);
add("development-policy-mix", "4.10", "core", "发展战略组合与证据评价\tDevelopment policy mixes and evidence",
 "有效战略应针对主要约束，结合市场激励与公共投入，按公平、可持续性、成本和可观察结果评价。\tEffective strategies target binding constraints, combine market incentives with public investment, and are evaluated through equity, sustainability, cost and observed outcomes.",
 "识别约束与目标；选择互补政策并明确时序；用可信结果证据修正措施\tIdentify constraints and goals; choose complementary policies and sequencing; revise measures using credible outcome evidence",
 "原创假设：出口加工需要道路、供电、技能与海关协同；设立对照或分期实施有助判断效果，还应检查地区和性别受益差异。\tHypothetical scenario: export processing needs roads, power, skills and customs coordination. Comparison groups or phased introduction help assess effects, alongside regional and gender differences.",
 "没有适用于所有国家的唯一配方；投入和宣布不能替代结果证据。\tThere is no single recipe for every country; spending and announcements cannot replace outcome evidence.",
 "怎样最能判断战略是否有效？\tHow can a strategy's effectiveness best be assessed?", "结合基线、可比结果与分配影响\tCombine baselines, comparable outcomes and distributional effects", ["只按计划支出排名\tRank only planned spending", "复制他国全部政策\tCopy every policy from another country", "忽略机会成本\tIgnore opportunity cost"], ["约束|constraints", "政策|policies", "证据|evidence"], ["20", "20.9", 633]);
export { topics };
